From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:27:16 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: Use the mainline dma_fence abstraction

Completion fences now come from one FenceContext in the device data,
built with new_unordered() so that each submission keeps a timeline of
its own as before. The execution holds the signaling side behind a lock
and signals it once, from whichever path finishes the job first.

Waits use Fence::wait_timeout() and timeline points come from
drm::syncobj::FenceChain.

Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
